<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka development banks dip on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka development banks dip on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Development Finance Corporation and National Development Bank Ltd fell in early profit-taking on Wednesday, brokers said.</p>
<p>DFCC fell 1.69 percent or five rupees to 290 rupees and NDB dropped 1.92 percent or five rupees to 255.</p>
<p>&quot;It is probably a small investor taking profit in the two blue chips,&quot; said a broker who declined to be identified.</p>
<p>DFCC and NDB are blue chip development finance institutions listed in Colombo.</p>
<p>-- Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
